# AI & Document Intelligence — VTC Apps

Apply when the app uses chat, RAG, embeddings, document ingestion, speech-to-text, or text-to-speech.

**Closed decisions** (one label, a yes/no, a score) use TypeSafe Jev in ZAPI — `jev-decisions.mdc`. Do not use chat models to classify a fixed set.

**Static Vite apps:** do not hold provider keys — call the ZAPI proxy `POST /apps/ai/chat|embeddings|rerank` with the user JWT (`nextjs-to-vite.mdc`). This file covers **Next.js** server-side provider access.

**Billing:** space owner pays **2× wholesale** from personal wallet — `platform-metering.mdc`. Price vars are platform-injected (`CREDITS_CHARGE_MULTIPLIER`, `DEEPINFRA_*_PRICE_PER_M`, etc.). MapTiler is not metered.

**All LLM keys are platform-injected at build** — do not commit `DEEPINFRA_*` or `AI_*` provider vars to `.env.production` (`env-development.mdc`). Set copies in `env_development` only for local testing.

**Server-side only** — never expose API keys to the browser (`NEXT_PUBLIC_` / `VITE_`).

---

## Provider: DeepInfra only

**DeepInfra is the only LLM provider on VTC** (Mark, 2026-10-17). **Groq and Cerebras are retired:** their keys are revoked and the build server strips any `GROQ_*` / `CEREBRAS_*` / `AI_GROQ_*` / `AI_CEREBRAS_*` vars from builds. Do not add `groq.ts`, `cerebras.ts`, `groq-sdk`, or api.groq.com / api.cerebras.ai URLs. If you find them in an existing app, replace them with the DeepInfra client below.

| Use | Model ID | Env var (injected) | Wholesale per 1M tokens |
|-----|----------|--------------------|-------------------------|
| **Fast chat / tool calls / JSON** (default) | `openai/gpt-oss-120b-Turbo` | `DEEPINFRA_CHAT_MODEL` | $0.15 in / $0.60 out (`DEEPINFRA_CHAT_INPUT_PRICE_PER_M` / `DEEPINFRA_CHAT_OUTPUT_PRICE_PER_M`) |
| Cheap chat / summaries | `Qwen/Qwen3-32B` | `DEEPINFRA_INFERENCE_MODEL` | $0.08 in / $0.28 out (`DEEPINFRA_INFERENCE_*_PRICE_PER_M`) |
| Tiny / high-volume | `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-Turbo` | set in app code | $0.02 in / $0.04 out |

`AI_DEFAULT_PROVIDER` is always `deepinfra`. Replacements for old model IDs: Cerebras `gpt-oss-120b` → `openai/gpt-oss-120b-Turbo`; Groq `qwen/qwen3-32b` → `Qwen/Qwen3-32B`; Groq `llama-3.1-8b-instant` → `meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-Turbo`; `llama-3.3-70b` → `meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Turbo`.

Use the **Turbo** gpt-oss tier — the base `openai/gpt-oss-120b` tier is often "Model busy" (429) and much slower.

**Reasoning:** send `reasoning_effort: "low"` for gpt-oss (env `DEEPINFRA_REASONING_EFFORT`, default `low`). For Qwen3 send `reasoning_effort: "none"` unless you need thinking — it is ~3× faster. If `message.content` is empty, fall back to `message.reasoning_content`.

**Tool calls:** DeepInfra accepts OpenAI `tools` / `tool_choice` on both gpt-oss-120b-Turbo and Qwen3-32B. Keep tool names to `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]` (map `a.b` → `a__b` and back).

```typescript
// src/lib/deepinfra.ts — DeepInfra chat (OpenAI-compatible)
const BASE = `${(process.env.DEEPINFRA_API_URL || 'https://api.deepinfra.com').replace(/\/$/, '')}/v1/openai`
export const CHAT_MODEL = process.env.DEEPINFRA_CHAT_MODEL || 'openai/gpt-oss-120b-Turbo'

export async function chat(messages: { role: string; content: string }[], model = CHAT_MODEL) {
  const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/chat/completions`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.DEEPINFRA_API_KEY}`,
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      model,
      messages,
      ...(model.includes('gpt-oss')
        ? { reasoning_effort: process.env.DEEPINFRA_REASONING_EFFORT || 'low' }
        : { reasoning_effort: 'none' }),
    }),
  })
  const data = await res.json()
  const msg = data.choices?.[0]?.message
  return { content: msg?.content || msg?.reasoning_content || '', usage: data.usage, model }
}
```

Bill with the price vars for the model you actually called (`platform-metering.mdc`).

